 "_comment": "The Capitol broadcast. Device: the poster window. A pristine commemorative poster for the Second Quarter Quell, built with no lettering at all: ivory paper, double gold rules, a gold Capitol sunburst, and one severe window that holds every image (Snow, Effie, Caesar, Drusilla, Magno, Plutarch, the reaping as ceremony, the tributes in their white parade suits). On bar 5 the window's edge becomes the frame: a hard cut to full bleed shows what the broadcast crops out (two tributes facing a wall of fire, then a scream), and on the next beat the poster is back as if nothing happened.",
